\f1\fs22 Sarah felt a breeze on her face. None of the windows or balcony doors were open. The door to the hall clicked. Sarah\'92s head snapped around, expecting Hayley. Who else could it be?\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91Hello, Sarah.\'92 A whisper from a shadow within the hooded robe of a medieval monk.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91You!\'92 Sarah was on her feet, ready for conflict, by word or deed, or both.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91Me,\'92 the crazy sage, Kleoboulos Windus, allowed. \'91Please don\'92t scream.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Sarah was offended. The idea she might call out for help presupposed a sense of vulnerability she had never experienced.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91How did you get in here? How did you get 
\f2\i here
\f1\i0 ?\'92\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo shrugged. \'91I have a gift of infiltrating places unnoticed.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah felt a threat in his confidence. And something his presence: something about the the light in the room made Kleo appear more apparition than physical, somewhere between corporeal flesh and blood, and grandaddy  poltergeist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No, I am a real man,\'92 Kleo said, guessing her thoughts. \'91What you sense as a quality of otherworldliness is a product of my weariness.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Yes, perhaps it was weariness that gave the impression he wasn\'92t all there. Sarah felt no threat from him. \'91You can\'92t hurt me, old man.\'92\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl2\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Kleo smiled and tented his fingers together. \'91Feeling invincible is not the same as being invincible. Catastrophic trauma would end you as easily as any other \'85\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91Are you here to kill me?\'92\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx1680\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91I am here to offer you life, and my service.\'92 Kleo took two gliding steps towards Sarah.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91You\'92ve made my life Hell!\'92 she hissed, aware Kathy sleeping. She could complicate an already unpredictable circumstance.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91I am truly sorry for the way you became pregnant. It was wrong. I wanted, needed your consent. Others thought your enrolment surplus to requirements.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\'91Convenient. Just blame some other lunatic in your cult.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Kleo appeared genuinely wounded by Sarah\'92s words. Feeling she was gaining the upper hand, she pressed. \'91Tell me the truth. Did Tony have any part in getting me pregnant?\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Kleo shook his head. \'91No. He has his part to play in coming events, but as to your pregnancy, he\'92s blameless. Ignorant, to be more accurate, and therefore as innocent as a newborn lamb.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Sarah felt her eyes misting. Tears came.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Kleo stepped closer and cradled Sarah\'92s cheek. \'91Oh, young Sarah, Tony Supaporn is not lost to you. There are wheels within wheels, and he will cycle back around many times yet before this is all done.\'92\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Sarah felt the weight of everything fall on her. She recoiled from Kleo\'92s embrace, and collapsed on the arm of the chair shed been sitting in only minutes before. She wiped the moisture from her face. \'91Why me?\'92 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re special, young Sarah,\'92 Kleo whispered, a raspy voice of empathy and compassion.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah grimaced at being called young. She read Kleo\'92s face. \'91You know. You know how I\'92m special.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After a moment, Kleo admitted, \'91I do.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91All part of the prophecy, I suppose.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Even at a whisper, Kleo could hear her bitterness. \'91It is.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Do you know how I became special?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The sage nodded sagely. \'91I believe so.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There are better times ahead for revealing such things,\'92 he said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Then you should leave.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I am here to give you comfort and succour.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re doing a taxing shit job of it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Young Sarah. I know how invested you are in your self-identity, your ability to rise above all obstacles.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I can look after myself.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo wobbled his head. \'91Mostly. Until you can\'92t.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91So taking me down a peg is your way of giving me comfort and succour?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91In a way, yes. Your \'85 talents \'85 have carried you this far. But now it\'92s time to accept assistance from any quarter.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You mean Eloise.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo nodded. \'91And others.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re telling me to marry Alexander.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It\'92s consistent with the prophecy.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, well if it\'92s consistent \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I think you will find the marriage will be a public shell only.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How would you know?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo made puckered shapes with his mouth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It\'92s consistent with the prophecy,\'92 Sarah said for him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Talk it out with Eloise. Do what you do so well: gather the facts, weigh the options.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What is so important about my baby anyway?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92ll be ushering in an age of enlightenment. One in which science and reason triumphs over technology and superstition.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And greed?\'92 Sarah found herself asking. It surprised her.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ultimately, it\'92s always bout greed.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And what of the Elvi?\'92 she asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I think you can see they are faring rather well.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Will that continue?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes. You will see to it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And that\'92s part of the prophecy, is it?\'92 Sarah asked sceptically.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Not so much,\'92 Kleo conceded. \'91Not nearly as much as it is part of you.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah started tearing up again. 
\f2\i These taxing Elvi! Why do I care about them
\f1\i0 ?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Everyone will be better off.\'92 Kleo emphasised by connecting matching fingertips and rocking his hands in front of his navel. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah nodded. She liked that. It gave her a purpose, and certainty she had never felt before. \'91So this is why I\'92m here?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91One of the things, certainly.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah set her jaw. \'91\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 I\'92m still not letting you off for the evil shit you did to me.\'92\
\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 The burden of your scorn is a weight I am willing to bear.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah could bear it no longer. Her tears were clogging her up. She raced for the bed and wiped her face on a sheet. Blinked away tears until her sight returned.\
\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo was gone. Sarah wasn\'92t sure she\'92d heard the door open or close.
